<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jangir Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1801–1845</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Zhangir Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jangir Khan was khan of the Bukey Horde, the Kazakh Inner Horde between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> and Ural rivers, from 1823 until his death. The son of its founder Bukey, he ruled under Russian protection, built a capital at Khan Ordasy, opened a school and encouraged trade fairs. His grants of land to his supporters provoked the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isatay-taimanuly">Isatay Taimanuly</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/makhambet-otemisuly">Makhambet Otemisuly</a> in 1836–1838. After his death <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> did not appoint a successor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jangir-khan.jpg" alt="Jangir Khan" width="196" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ibrometeor · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A1%D0%B0%D0%BB%D2%9B%D0%B0%D0%BC_%D0%96%D3%99%D2%A3%D0%B3%D1%96%D1%80_%D1%85%D0%B0%D0%BD.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
